100 REM CREATE ARTICLES DATABASE
110 PRINT CHR$(4)"OPEN ARTICLES.DATA"
120 PRINT CHR$(4)"WRITE ARTICLES.DATA"
130 PRINT "APPLE COMPUTER"
140 PRINT "The Apple II is a personal computer designed by Steve Wozniak."
150 PRINT "It was released June 16, 1977 and sold for $666.66."
160 PRINT "Features: 1 MHz 6502 processor, 4-64KB RAM, color graphics."
170 PRINT "The Apple II family became one of the most popular computers of the 1980s."
180 PRINT "~"
190 PRINT "DOS 3.3"
200 PRINT "DOS 3.3 is the standard operating system for Apple II computers."
210 PRINT "It manages 5.25 inch floppy disk storage and provides a command line."
220 PRINT "Features: 16 sectors per track, 140KB total capacity per disk."
230 PRINT "DOS 3.3 supports both sequential and random file access."
240 PRINT "~"
250 PRINT "APPLESOFT BASIC"
260 PRINT "Applesoft BASIC is the primary programming language for Apple II."
270 PRINT "It includes graphics commands like PLOT, HLIN, VLIN for drawing."
280 PRINT "Also supports sound synthesis, joystick input, and shape tables."
290 PRINT "Thousands of programs were written in Applesoft BASIC during the 1980s."
300 PRINT "~"
310 PRINT "FLOPPY DISK STORAGE"
320 PRINT "The 5.25 inch floppy disk is the primary storage for Apple II."
330 PRINT "Standard DOS 3.3 disk holds 140KB of data on both sides."
340 PRINT "Disks use 35 tracks with 16 sectors per track."
350 PRINT "Floppy drives were the main way to share and distribute software."
360 PRINT "~"
370 PRINT "MACHINE LANGUAGE"
380 PRINT "Machine language is the fastest way to program Apple II computers."
390 PRINT "Written in 6502 assembly language for direct processor control."
390 PRINT "Can be called from BASIC programs for performance-critical code."
400 PRINT "Most games and utilities use machine language for speed."
410 PRINT "~"
420 PRINT CHR$(4)"CLOSE"
430 PRINT "DATABASE SAVED AS ARTICLES.DATA"
440 END
